// CotSC: English translation extracted from bg0104_baldurs_gate.d
// Original English strings preserved exactly. Translate text inside ~...~ only.

@1 = ~Had roles be reversed, I wouldn't barge into your room. I expect some common decency.~
@2 = ~Ehm... my... my name is Leyala.~
@3 = ~(She blushes.) How charming of you, Sir Coran.~
@4 = ~Coran. Maybe keep what little you have in your pants for the time being?~
@5 = ~Unbelievable.~
@6 = ~Good day to you, then.~
@7 = ~I hope you don't make it a habit, <CHARNAME>, to roam around people's rooms. Wouldn't be the first time, though I held my tongue so far.~
@8 = ~It is far beyond the known edges of common decency to meet a young woman who moves with such grace. May I learn your name?~
@9 = ~Coran, m'lady. It is stunningly quaint to meet you. Your rare, exotic beauty complements those wondrous eyes.~
@10 = ~Only a compliment, my friend. I meant no offence to the lady.~
@11 = ~One can hardly blame me for admiring beauty. Still, perhaps we've overstayed our welcome.~
